  "Question": "Let \\(x\\) be the number\n\n\\[0.\\underbrace{0000\\ldots00001}_{1996 \\text{ zeros}},\\]\n\nwhere there are \\(1996\\) zeros after the decimal point. Which of the following expressions represents the largest number?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3 + x\\)",
    "B": "\\(3 - x\\)",
    "C": "\\(3 \\cdot x\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac{3}{x}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\frac{x}{3}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The decimal has a nonzero digit far to the right, so \\(0<x<0.1\\). Its exact value is unnecessary. Multiplying this bound by \\(30\\) gives \\(30x<3\\). Since \\(x>0\\), we may divide by \\(x\\) to obtain\n\\[\n\\frac3x>30.\n\\]\nFor the other four choices,\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n3+x&<3.1, & 3-x&<3,\\\\\n3x&<0.3, & \\frac{x}{3}&<0.1.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nEvery other choice is therefore smaller than \\(3/x\\). The largest expression is \\(\\frac3x\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
